add('c0309','lastcuentista-awake-collective-zero','The Last Cuentista (the awake Collective-controlled ship)','The Last Cuentista','The functioning takeover order aboard the ship','Active awake living human ship residents','Stasis, preserved people and memory erasure do not automatically create leisure residents; the Collective is not assumed unrelated AI.',
'''The ship’s takeover suppresses human memory while preserving a technically managed habitat. The guarantee best guess is mixed and conditional: life-support can sustain residents while authority controls their identities, access and duties. The point concerns active awake residents rather than sleepers or a hypothetical completed destination society. Automated environmental support is material infrastructure, but it does not prove universal freedom from useful work.

 Concentrated human Collective authority places control near the non-AI elite reference point, with machine-management alternatives inside the interval. Memory control is not by itself evidence that every ruler is an autonomous AI. This zero variant counts operations, cultivation, cleaning, maintenance, administration, care and assigned work. A lost personal history does not erase a person’s participation. The low nonworking scenario preserves unknown roles without calculating leisure from stasis duration. Broad bounds keep ordinary allocation uncertain while retaining the recognizable controlled generation-ship order and avoiding an unshown uniform colonial constitution.''',
(.25,.02,.15),([-.9,.99],[-.85,.6],[0,.95]),('Managed habitat support coexists with controlled identity and duties.','Concentrated human Collective authority is central with technical alternatives.','Useful and assigned awake-person roles count; stasis is excluded.'),
['The publisher describes a shipboard takeover and suppression of human memory.'],['Active awake people define the cohort; exact ordinary rights remain estimates.','The Collective is not automatically an unrelated AI sovereign.'],'Retain the recognizable controlled ship habitat as an awake-population zero variant.')

last=add('c0310','lasthuman-bacon-active-robot-city-zero','The Last Human (Lee Bacon’s active robot civilization)','The Last Human','The functioning robot world when an unexpected human is encountered','Active conscious robot residents in the Lee Bacon continuity','The unexpected human and hidden survivor claims are separate; Zack Jordan’s same-titled novel is not this setting.',
'''The robot world includes working artificial persons who encounter a human they believed impossible. The retained point is their own active technical society, not an assertion that one protected survivor establishes universal human welfare. The guarantee best guess allows substantial internal support, qualified by unknown resource rights and institutional constraints. Belief in humanity’s elimination is not treated as a literal human leisure denominator.

 Control is strongly independent of organic owners, with internal hierarchy and restrictive rules inside the interval. This zero variant counts useful production, services, operations, maintenance, administration, care and public creation performed by robot persons. Private learning is not automatically a job, while robot embodiment does not make everyone a nonworker. The modest nonworking scenario remains broad because the short publisher account is not a labor census. The record explicitly uses a conscious synthetic-person proxy and keeps mechanisms, stored data and the separate human encounter outside that counted population.''',
(-.3,-.85,.25),([-.99,.95],[-1,.65],[0,.98]),('A functioning robot society permits support with ordinary coverage uncertain.','Organic-owner independence is strong with internal constraints.','Useful active synthetic roles count; claimed human absence is not leisure.'),
['The publisher describes working robots encountering an unexpected human in Lee Bacon’s novel.'],['Active conscious robots define the synthetic-person proxy.','Internal material rights and participation remain estimates.'],'Retain the identifiable active robot society with the original human-preservation lead corrected.',regime=5,proxy=True)
